<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh 12-mth T-bill av yield eases to 15.35 pct.</title>
<headline>Kazakh 12-mth T-bill av yield eases to 15.35 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on an issue of 12-month MKM discount Treasury bills edged down to 15.35 percent annual at an auction on Monday from 15.74 percent at the last auction on June 2, the National Bank said. Details of the auction:</p>
<p>					   July 14	    July 2</p>
<p> Series number			 KZ4CK1607985     KZ4CK0406983</p>
<p> Issue volume (million tenge)	  600		  450</p>
<p> Bids (nominal, million tenge)	 1,950		2,530</p>
<p> Sold (nominal, million tenge)	 600		  460</p>
<p> Average price			 86.69 pct	  86.40</p>
<p> Average yield			 15.35 pct	  15.74</p>
<p> Tenor				   364 days	   364 days</p>
<p> Maturity				July 16, 1997    June 4, 1998</p>
<p>($1 = 75.2005 tenge)</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
